      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The debate around the \"win versus loss\" of EPA mandates is very real, with strong arguments on both sides in the industry. Proponents argue the strict rules are necessary to curb pollution and fulfill necessary public health and environmental protection. However, many small manufacturers feel the associated compliance and capital investment costs are disproportionately high, effectively favoring larger, more heavily capitalized corporations and leading to market exit for smaller, established local firms.",
      "source": "target",
